Due to time constraints, only selected items of the UEQ were asked: one item “goodbad” for the dimension attractiveness and all items for the dimension perspicuity. Results are shown in Fig. 5. Although mean ratings differ, those results are not statistical signiﬁcant, neither on attractiveness (F value: 2.257, sig.: p = 0.069; partial eta sq.: 0.091) nor on perspicuity (F value: 2.219, sig.: p = 0.073; partial eta sq.: 0.090).

